** Prologue (Character Generation and Initial Strategy) **



   How I intend to play Elryk:

 - Elryk is going to be a chaotic elven wizard, the closest equivilant
in Nethack that I can find for him.

 - Elryk will also be male. This is the first time that I'll be
playing an intelligent character of the masculin gender. <laugh!> This
is a deviation from my normal way of role playing.

 - Elryk will be; patient in execution of the mission, skillful with
how he developes his abilities, but mostly cunning when faced with
foes.

 - Elryk will not be paying attention to the vertical axis of
alignment (there isn't one in Nethack any way). Good, neutral, or
evil. None shall I hold in preference. Instead: Whichever will best
achieve my goals - at whatever point in time - shall be the one I
pursue.

 - Elryk will try to please Anhur in many ways. Hopefully to one day
become the "Glory of Arioch". This (I believe) is necessary in order
to be able to wield the runesword "Stormbringer".

 - Elryk will offer enough creatures worthy of Anhur's might, and be
granted the gift of the most powerful artifact in the multiverse; the
runesword "Stormbringer". Upon which he plans to use it mercilessly,
and without remorse (in order to take souls in the name of Anhur).

 - Elryk will not let anyone or anything stand in his way. Demons will
be dealt with just as much despise, as devils, or angels, should they
be foolish enough to try and get in his way.

 - Elryk will retrieve the amulet (or die in the attempt) for Anhur.
Not because he wishes Anhur to become more powerful than the rest of
the gods, but because after doing so, Elryk will be free from
servitude!



